        "body": "### Describe the feature you'd like to request\n\n## TL;DR\n\nAdd bookmark shortcuts as a searchable source in Homarr's search bar / command palette.\nUsers can type an alias like `irc`, see `TheLounge`, and open the URL immediately \u2014\nwithout needing a full app entry or dashboard placement first.\n\n## Why this would help\n\nRight now, adding a lightweight link requires several steps: create an App, add it to\nBookmarks, then place it visually on the board. For internal tools and frequently used\nlinks, that's more overhead than the link warrants.\n\nThis would be especially useful for:\n\n- internal or self-hosted tools that don't need a full app entry\n- shared or family boards where people remember names better than layouts\n- users coming from simpler, bookmark-focused dashboards\n\n## Use cases\n\n- `irc` \u2192 TheLounge\n- `requests` \u2192 Jellyseerr\n- `books` \u2192 Audiobookshelf\n- `indexers` \u2192 Prowlarr\n- `1337x` \u2192 specific Prowlarr indexer entry\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nAdd bookmarks or shortcuts as a searchable source in the command palette. Each shortcut\nwould look something like this:\n\n- **Name:** `TheLounge`\n- **Aliases:** `irc`, `chat`, `thelounge`\n- **URL:** `https://thelounge.example.com`\n- **Icon**\n- **Description**\n- **Open in new tab** toggle\n- **Permission / group visibility**\n- **Tags or folder/group** (optional)\n\n### What I\u2019d want it to do\n\n- Typing an alias or name returns matching shortcuts\n- Pressing Enter opens the selected result directly\n- Fuzzy matching works across both name and aliases\n- Results respect existing visibility and permission rules\n\n### Optional / nice-to-have\n\n- Show hostname or description beneath each result\n- Group results by type (Apps / Bookmarks / Search Engines / Integrations)\n- Allow shortcuts to appear above generic web search results\n- Full keyboard-first navigation and launching\n\n## Stretch goals\n\n**Reuse existing App entries as shortcuts** (already done)\nPull from existing App entries to avoid duplicating data for tools already on the board.\n\n**Quick-add bookmark shortcut**\nA lightweight flow to add a URL, name, and alias without going through the full widget\nsetup \u2014 useful for one-off or infrequently visited links.\n\n**Prowlarr import**\nImport Prowlarr-managed entries as searchable shortcuts, so indexers and related tools\nare reachable directly from the command palette. A simple manual import would be a\nreasonable starting point.\n\n\n### Additional information\n\nThis would complement the existing App and Bookmarks model rather than replace it.\n\nFocus search would work great in conjunction with this. https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/3595\nSlighly related to: https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/3314",
